{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "14466444",
      "title": "Adding Auto-Login",
      "lectureOrder": 629,
      "videoOrder": 580,
      "sourceHash": "2849c1e06442cece7bb41a9dc2b6dea7c08c882b118db393ac14bd351308e681",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.19,
          "end": 4.95,
          "en": "Instructor: We got the general authentication flow",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.95,
          "end": 5.79,
          "en": "up and running.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.79,
          "end": 8.653,
          "en": "While we're not protecting unauthenticated access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.653,
          "end": 11.85,
          "en": "to the recipes route, we'll do so soon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.85,
          "end": 13.44,
          "en": "First of all though, I wanna make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.44,
          "end": 15.66,
          "en": "that once we are authenticated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.66,
          "end": 17.37,
          "en": "we don't just keep that status",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.37,
          "end": 20.73,
          "en": "as long as we're navigating around in the app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 20.73,
          "end": 23.82,
          "en": "but that we also keep that status, that we also keep",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 23.82,
          "end": 26.19,
          "en": "that token, which we have once",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 26.19,
          "end": 27.72,
          "en": "we reload the page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 27.72,
          "end": 29.58,
          "en": "Because at the moment, when we reload the page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 29.58,
          "end": 31.29,
          "en": "we lose all that status.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 31.29,
          "end": 32.94,
          "en": "Because when you reload the page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 32.94,
          "end": 35.19,
          "en": "your angle or application restarts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 35.19,
          "end": 37.737,
          "en": "The old one is basically dumped.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 37.737,
          "end": 41.28,
          "en": "And since right now we're managing everything in memory,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 41.28,
          "end": 44.4,
          "en": "remember that we're storing the token in a user model",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 44.4,
          "end": 46.993,
          "en": "which happens in JavaScript only in which therefore happens",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 46.993,
          "end": 48.15,
          "en": "in memory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 48.15,
          "end": 48.983,
          "en": "Since we managed it all in memory,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 48.983,
          "end": 52.349,
          "en": "we'll lose all that state whenever the application restarts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 52.349,
          "end": 55.29,
          "en": "because that memory gets cleared automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 55.29,
          "end": 57.24,
          "en": "There is no connection between the last time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 57.24,
          "end": 59.4,
          "en": "we ran this Angular app on this webpage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 59.4,
          "end": 60.75,
          "en": "and the current time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 60.75,
          "end": 63.78,
          "en": "So there is no connection and the memory is lost.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 63.78,
          "end": 65.58,
          "en": "So if you wanna store that token,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 65.58,
          "end": 68.163,
          "en": "we have to store it somewhere else and not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 68.163,
          "end": 71.7,
          "en": "in a JavaScript Variable or class property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 71.7,
          "end": 75.21000000000001,
          "en": "We have to store it in a persistent storage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 75.21000000000001,
          "end": 79.17,
          "en": "that survives page reloads and browser restarts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 79.17,
          "end": 82.47,
          "en": "that we can write to and that we can fetch data from.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 82.47,
          "end": 85.05,
          "en": "Now what would be such a storage?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 85.05,
          "end": 87.27,
          "en": "In a browser, you got different storages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 87.27,
          "end": 91.14,
          "en": "You can't access the normal file system on your device,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 91.14,
          "end": 95.58,
          "en": "but you can work with cookies or with local storage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 95.58,
          "end": 98.16,
          "en": "which is an API exposed by the browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 98.16,
          "end": 102.27000000000001,
          "en": "to store simple key value pairs basically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 102.27000000000001,
          "end": 105.36,
          "en": "on the file system but controlled by the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 105.36,
          "end": 110.22,
          "en": "And we will use local storage here to store that token.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 110.22,
          "end": 112.10499999999999,
          "en": "To do that, let's go to the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 112.10499999999999,
          "end": 114.27000000000001,
          "en": "handle authentication method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 114.27000000000001,
          "end": 116.94,
          "en": "in the off service, which is where we do create",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 116.94,
          "end": 120.33,
          "en": "our user object and emit it to our application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 120.33,
          "end": 123.66,
          "en": "And there, besides emitting it to the application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 123.66,
          "end": 126.87,
          "en": "we also wanna store it in our storage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 126.87,
          "end": 131.49,
          "en": "And for that, you can simply use local storage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 131.49,
          "end": 134.46,
          "en": "and call set item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 134.46,
          "end": 138.21,
          "en": "This allows you to write an item to the local storage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 138.21,
          "end": 140.37,
          "en": "and to store data there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 140.37,
          "end": 143.37,
          "en": "Now there, I will give this a name of user data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 143.37,
          "end": 144.81,
          "en": "And this name is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 144.81,
          "end": 146.57999999999998,
          "en": "This is basically the key by which",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 146.57999999999998,
          "end": 148.5,
          "en": "you will be able to retrieve it later",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 148.5,
          "end": 152.4,
          "en": "and then you have to write some data to that key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 152.4,
          "end": 154.98,
          "en": "You can store some data there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 154.98,
          "end": 157.05,
          "en": "Now the data I wanna store there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 157.05,
          "end": 158.97,
          "en": "should just be that user object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 158.97,
          "end": 160.59,
          "en": "because that contains all the data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 160.59,
          "end": 161.43,
          "en": "I want to save.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 161.43,
          "end": 163.29,
          "en": "The email, the user ID, the token,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 163.29,
          "end": 164.61,
          "en": "and the expiration date,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 164.61,
          "end": 166.9,
          "en": "these are the pieces of data I wanna store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 166.9,
          "end": 170.22,
          "en": "So we can write the user to the local storage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 170.22,
          "end": 171.69,
          "en": "though not like that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 171.69,
          "end": 173.64,
          "en": "not as a JavaScript object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 173.64,
          "end": 176.76,
          "en": "Instead, we have to convert it to a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 176.76,
          "end": 178.8,
          "en": "We can do that with the JSON object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 178.8,
          "end": 182.28,
          "en": "and the stringify method that is built into JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 182.28,
          "end": 185.61,
          "en": "and it simply serializes a JavaScript object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 185.61,
          "end": 187.65,
          "en": "It converts a JavaScript object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 187.65,
          "end": 191.97,
          "en": "to a string version of it, so to say, so to text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 191.97,
          "end": 195.42,
          "en": "And that text is getting stored in the local storage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 195.42,
          "end": 196.8,
          "en": "Let me show you how this works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 196.8,
          "end": 200.00900000000001,
          "en": "If we save that, and the application therefore restarts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 200.00900000000001,
          "end": 203.583,
          "en": "If we go to authenticate and we do log in here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 204.81,
          "end": 206.07,
          "en": "it works as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 206.07,
          "end": 208.2,
          "en": "But now in the Chrome DevTools,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 208.2,
          "end": 211.44,
          "en": "if you go to the application tab there, you can go",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 211.44,
          "end": 216.12,
          "en": "to local storage and expand this and there pick your storage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 216.12,
          "end": 218.61,
          "en": "and you should see that user data key there now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 218.61,
          "end": 220.95,
          "en": "And in there, you find that data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 220.95,
          "end": 222.81,
          "en": "you just saved to the storage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 222.81,
          "end": 224.55,
          "en": "And this is all text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 224.55,
          "end": 227.73,
          "en": "it's the JavaScript object converted to a text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 227.73,
          "end": 231.36,
          "en": "Hence you there see the email, you see the long token,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 231.36,
          "end": 233.25,
          "en": "you see the token expiration date.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 233.25,
          "end": 236.7,
          "en": "All of that is stored in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 236.7,
          "end": 239.19,
          "en": "Now, with all of that being stored in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 239.19,
          "end": 241.26,
          "en": "we can of course also retrieve it from there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 241.26,
          "end": 243.63,
          "en": "when our application restarts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 243.63,
          "end": 246.24,
          "en": "For that, we can add a new method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 246.24,
          "end": 248.43,
          "en": "which I will name auto login",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 248.43,
          "end": 250.59,
          "en": "because it basically is a method that will try",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 250.59,
          "end": 253.35,
          "en": "to automatically set the user to log in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 253.35,
          "end": 255.84,
          "en": "when the application starts and it will do so",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 255.84,
          "end": 257.79,
          "en": "by looking into the storage and checking",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 257.79,
          "end": 261.96,
          "en": "whether there is an existing user snapshot stored.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 261.96,
          "end": 265.74,
          "en": "So in auto login, the goal now will be to retrieve data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 265.74,
          "end": 267.6,
          "en": "from the local storage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 267.6,
          "end": 269.65,
          "en": "For that, we can access the local storage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 270.677,
          "end": 273.06,
          "en": "and get our user data item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 273.06,
          "end": 276.3,
          "en": "And that is a synchronous method which gives us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 276.3,
          "end": 277.68,
          "en": "our user data like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 277.68,
          "end": 278.97,
          "en": "So we can retrieve user data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 278.97,
          "end": 281.49,
          "en": "from local storage just like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 281.49,
          "end": 284.67,
          "en": "The first thing which I'll do then is I will check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 284.67,
          "end": 286.02,
          "en": "whether that exists.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 286.02,
          "end": 288.06,
          "en": "If we don't have user data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 288.06,
          "end": 293.06,
          "en": "so if this is false ish, we can return because in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 293.67,
          "end": 295.44,
          "en": "well, we can't lock the user in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 295.44,
          "end": 296.85,
          "en": "There is no stored user data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 296.85,
          "end": 300.6,
          "en": "So the user definitely needs to sign in on his own.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 300.6,
          "end": 304.86,
          "en": "Otherwise, if we make it past this check, user data is set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 304.86,
          "end": 307.65,
          "en": "and there is some snapshot we were able to retrieve",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 307.65,
          "end": 310.32,
          "en": "from that local storage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 310.32,
          "end": 312.69,
          "en": "Now important, the snapshot we're retrieving here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 312.69,
          "end": 314.73,
          "en": "is also a string because we're saving it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 314.73,
          "end": 316.02,
          "en": "as a string down there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 316.02,
          "end": 317.7,
          "en": "And therefore, if we want to work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 317.7,
          "end": 320.16,
          "en": "with that as a normal JavaScript object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 320.16,
          "end": 324.3,
          "en": "we have to convert it back by calling JSON parse here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 324.3,
          "end": 326.88,
          "en": "And this will simply just take the string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 326.88,
          "end": 328.8,
          "en": "and JSON format and convert it back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 328.8,
          "end": 330.39,
          "en": "into a JavaScript object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 330.39,
          "end": 332.28,
          "en": "Not into our user model though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 332.28,
          "end": 336.12,
          "en": "it will not have this token gather, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 336.12,
          "end": 337.98,
          "en": "but into a simple object literal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 337.98,
          "end": 341.55,
          "en": "which has all the keys that we stored in that storage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 341.55,
          "end": 344.43,
          "en": "So basically, this stringer converted back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 344.43,
          "end": 347.61,
          "en": "to a object literal in JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 347.61,
          "end": 351.21,
          "en": "With that, here in auto login,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 351.21,
          "end": 355.89,
          "en": "we can create a new loaded user by calling new user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 355.89,
          "end": 357.75,
